In article <30453@ucbvax.BERKELEY.EDU> wisner@mica.Berkeley.EDU (Bill Wisner, Libertine) writes:
>Let's face it. Wizards are wimps. And the junky equipment they get stuck
>with doesn't help much. So why not stop giving them junky equipment?

WHAT?!?  What version of NetHack are YOU playing??!!

When HACK (without the NET) originally had the Wizard class, he had NO weapons
and none of his magic items were identified.  This was why wizards always began
with a 16 strength: they needed something to help them overcome their severe
limitations.
   Now, though, ALL of their magic items are identified, they get a dagger to
start out with, and they even get a couple of spellbooks (which weren't in the
code before).  This, coupled with the ability to ^T teleport at 6th level
rather than 10th (and, I believe, immunity to magic traps, though I might be
wrong on this) makes the Wizard one of the most devastating character classes
to play, second only to a caveman or a class that starts out with a katana.
(The katana itself isn't all that powerful, unless you name it something....)
With all their extra stuff, I'd lower them to 13 or 14 strength if I were
upgrading the source code.

If you're going to complain about wimpy character classes, complain about
Archeologists and Healers (especially healers), not Wizards!


